Even apart from lojban I'd like to learn the IPA for the purpose of being
able to talk about accents via text (in emails and whatnot).

If I learnt german I would use  both german and loljban letters/words to
describe how I pronounce some things in english.  The more different ways
one can describe a thing, the less chance there is of confusion (because th=
e
more distinct ways you describe a thing, the narrower the possible scope of
that thing becomes).

love is like: <insert 5 million lines of poetry on the subject of love>.
 With each line the scope of the analogy becomes narrower.

